# .NET Build Outputs
bin/
obj/
TestResults/
# The README's publish recipe writes standalone builds here - see README.md.
out/

# OS/IDE generated files (Standard additions)
.DS_Store
.vs/
.vscode/

# DianaOS's runtime tree - see `man hier` - real, uncommitted data, not
# source. home/ IS the shell's root and holds all of it: Games, Saves,
# Firmware, Cheats, Logs, etc/EmuSen and tmp. The bare etc/, tmp/ and
# SourceLogs/ entries cover trees left by builds from before the move.
# *.srm/*.state cover saves still written outside it - the NES and Game
# Boy cores keep theirs beside the ROM for now, see EmuSen_Galaxia.md §6.
home/
etc/
tmp/
SourceLogs/
*.srm
*.state

# Coverage maps written by `cov save` (see `man cov`) - a recording of one
# person's playthrough of one ROM, accumulated locally and merged on load.
# Real, uncommitted data like the saves above, not source.
*.covmap

# Copyrighted commercial ROMs dropped here for local debugging/testing -
# never belongs in version control (redistribution), regardless of who
# added it or why.
TestRoms/
EmuSen.DianaOS/DianaOS/Usr/Home/Games/*
EmuSen.DianaOS/DianaOS/Usr/Home/Roms/*
!EmuSen.DianaOS/DianaOS/Usr/Home/Games/.gitkeep
!EmuSen.DianaOS/DianaOS/Usr/Home/Roms/.gitkeep
*.smc
*.sfc
*.nes

# Reference-emulator dumps written by the probe (see EmuSen.WiseMan/Reference),
# whichever backend produced them - the profile directories it sites beside them
# are named for that backend and are covered by the same rule.
# These are VRAM/OAM/GSU-RAM snapshots of a commercial game - the same
# redistribution rule as the ROMs above applies to state extracted from one.
EmuSen.WiseMan/Reference/dumps/

# Cargo's build output for the Rust probe. build-probe.sh directs it into the
# work dir instead, so this only catches a bare `cargo build` in the crate.
EmuSen.WiseMan/Reference/probe-rs/target/

# The libretro cheat database, downloaded at runtime - ~28k files and
# 250MB of CC BY-SA data that `cheat db update` fetches on demand. See
# `man cheat`.
EmuSen.DianaOS/DianaOS/Usr/Home/Cheats/

# Coprocessor firmware dumps (dsp1.rom, st010.program.rom, ...). Same rule
# as the ROMs above and for the same reason: the mask ROM inside a DSP-1 is
# Nintendo's, and a BIOS pack's own MIT/GPL license covers that pack's
# tooling, not the dumps it redistributes. See Venus_NecDSP.md §2.
EmuSen.DianaOS/DianaOS/Usr/Home/Firmware/*
!EmuSen.DianaOS/DianaOS/Usr/Home/Firmware/.gitkeep

# AI-assistant config. This repo does not carry one and must not depend on one -
# it has been added and deleted more than once. Ignored so it cannot come back.
CLAUDE.md

# Databases. The schema is committed and the .db is a build artifact - a binary
# cannot be reviewed and a schema is the part worth reviewing. Named one by one
# rather than globbed, so adding a database is a deliberate line here.
# See EmuSen_Stack.md §2.3.
known-differences.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
catalogue.db
dumps.db

# Python bytecode from the analysis tools.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The folder feed NuGet.config points at. EmuSen.LunaP is built from its own
# repository and is not this one's to carry.
local-packages/
